If there is a problem of dust box clogging, it is recommended that you turn on the pet mode in APP, if you are a multi-pet household, it is recommended that you set the dust collection frequency to 15min dust collection; clean the dust box & filter and restart the task;

Tips:

The Robot Vacuum will not perform dust collection during the Do Not Disturb time period, if you often perform the cleaning task during the Do Not Disturb time period, please manually clean the dust box and filter after cleaning;

Please find the link to the cleaning guide for the dust box and filter here:

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/How-to-clean-the-E25-E28-dust-box-filters.mp4

In Do Not Disturb mode, the machine will not perform dust collection but will perform suction. Suction is a mandatory function in mopping mode and is triggered by the omni station's fan, so noise issues may arise;

We recommend setting Do Not Disturb mode and using Sweep-Only Mode or starting cleaning before leaving home or resting, allowing dust collection tasks to be automatically completed during unoccupied periods;

Tips:

1. Dust collection will not be performed during Do Not Disturb mode. If you frequently perform cleaning tasks during Do Not Disturb mode, please manually clean the dustbin and filter after cleaning;

The video link below will guide you on how to clean the dust box filter.

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/How-to-clean-the-E25-E28-dust-box-filters.mp4

2. We fully understand that the noise generated during dust collection may affect your experience. This sound is a normal operation of the dust collection system. To thoroughly remove dust from the dustbin and compress it into the dust bag, a powerful suction force is required to operate the fan at high speed for a short period of time, which inevitably produces significant noise. This is an unavoidable process to achieve efficient dust collection under current technology and is not a machine malfunction;

