2.The software logic sets the dust collection to start only when the cleaning time is greater than 15 minutes to avoid noise caused by starting the base station during peak hours. If the cleaning time of a single task is less than 15 minutes, dust collection will be performed in the next task;

* 1. Open the dust collection station lid, take out the dust bag, and replace it with a new one (note: avoid reusing the dust bag, as the dust from the used dust bag will block the gaps in the bag fabric and cause false alarms);
* 
* 2. If the error message still appears after replacing the new dust bag, it may be that the dust collection air duct is blocked, and you need to check step by step:

a. Take out the dust box to check whether the dust box is blocked by garbage, causing dust collection failure, and clean the garbage in the dust box;

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/check-the-dust-collector.png

b. Check whether the dust collection air duct of the robot is blocked, and use tools to clean the blocked foreign objects;

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/Check-the-dust-collection-air-duct-of-the-robot-is-blocked.png

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/check-the-dust-collection-air-duct-of-the-robot.png

c. Check whether the dust collection air duct of the station is blocked, and use tools to clean the foreign objects that may be blocked in the entire channel;

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/check-the-dust-collection-air-duct-of-the-station.png

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/check-the-dust-collection-air-duct-of-the-station-part.png

Main troubleshooting step:

* 1.Check whether the side wheels are entangled with wires or hair; If so, clean up foreign objects, and ensure that the wheels rotate normally.





Additional Tips:

* 1.It is recommended to store the wires in advance before starting the cleaning task to avoid the side wheels getting stuck again;
* 2.The robot may get stuck on obstacles such as bar chairs and thresholds during the escape process. If the robot often reports that the side wheels are stuck in certain specific locations, it is recommended to create a no-go zone for the stuck area on the map;

* 1.Please empty the dirty water in the dirty water tank;
* 2.If the dirty water tank is empty and the error message still appears, please open the dirty water tank cover and check whether the float in the dirty water tank is still there and whether it moves up and down normally.

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/check-the-float.png

* 1.The noise from the machine may come from the fan, roller brush, side brush, side wheel, or mop pads;
* 2.If the fan noise is very sharp, remove the dust box, take out the filter, and check if the filter is severely clogged. Clean the filter and try again;

<https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/How-to-clean-the-dust-box-of-the-X10-Pro-Omni-T2351.mov>

* 3.If the noise comes from the roller brush, remove the roller brush and roller brush cover, and check if the roller brush is severely tangled with hair, especially at both ends; whether the comb teeth on the roller brush cover are jammed due to severe dust accumulation, clean them separately, and try again;

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/Cleaning-of-foreign-objects-and-hairs-from-the-ends-of-the-roller-brushes.mp4

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/How-to-clean-the-comb-teeth-of-the-X10-Pro-Omni-T2351.mp4

* 4.If the noise is coming from the side brush, remove the side brush and check if it is tangled with hair, clean it, and try again;

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/Remove-side-brush.png

* 5.If the noise is coming from the side wheel, check if the side wheel is tangled with foreign objects, clean it, and try again;

https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/Please-check-the-side-wheels.png

* 6.If the noise is coming from the mop pad, check if the mop pad holder assembly is cracked or damaged, accompanied by the mop bouncing up and down; (Note: When the mop pad is dry, there may be unusual sounds. In this case, please check the water outlet volume and mopping settings. For rooms larger than 25 square meters, do not select the by-room mopping frequency; instead, choose the 15-minute mopping frequency.)
https://d3pkbgk01oouhl.cloudfront.net/upload_file/prod/Check-the-mop-support-for-cracks.png

